# Open DJ desktop build-time budget. Single source of truth: sourced by both
# `just dmg` (self-measurement) and .agents/skills/ship-dmg/scripts/ship_dmg.sh
# (per-phase decomposition), so the two can never drift apart.
#
# THE SPLIT THAT MATTERS: gate what we control, monitor what we do not.
#
# The pipeline blocks synchronously on Apple TWICE per build -- `notarytool
# submit --wait` for the .app (justfile:1324) and again for the .dmg
# (justfile:1335). Apple's queue is unbounded and not a function of our code.
# A hard failure on TOTAL wall time would therefore fire on Apple's queue
# rather than on a regression we introduced, which trains everyone to ignore
# it. So the HARD gate covers only the controlled phases; the Apple phases get
# their own budget and can only ever FLAG.
#
# CALIBRATION (measured, Thu 10 Sep 2026):
#   - two reconstructed end-to-end builds: 694s (11m34s) and 308s (5m8s)
#   - cold cargo: 535s, from docs/research/webview-engine-and-crates-recommendations.md:230
#   - one measured notarization: 86s (sign_macos_developer_id.sh)
# Re-derive these rather than trusting the numbers above once ops/logs/ship-dmg.log
# carries real build rows; they are a starting ratchet, not a fixed truth.

# ---- controlled phases: payload, sign, cargo, bundle, compress, verify ----
# SOFT: report carries a FLAG and the run continues. Matches OPS-06's original
# 12-minute budget, which a 694s build already sits just inside.
BUILD_CONTROLLED_SOFT_S=720
# HARD: something is wrong with our build, not with Apple. Escalate; do not
# quietly ship. 25 min is ~2x the worst controlled build ever recorded here.
BUILD_CONTROLLED_HARD_S=1500

# ---- Apple notarization, per submission (app and dmg counted separately) ----
# FLAG ONLY at both levels. We cannot fix Apple's queue, but a sustained shift
# is worth knowing about because it changes how the ship lane should be paced.
BUILD_NOTARIZE_SOFT_S=300
BUILD_NOTARIZE_HARD_S=600

# ---- cargo ----
# At or above this, the cargo phase was a cold build (existing OPS-06 constant).
BUILD_CARGO_COLD_THRESHOLD_S=240
# A cold cargo above this is a regression in the build itself. Measured cold is
# 535s on a profile already at lto=true, codegen-units=1, opt-level="z".
BUILD_CARGO_COLD_SOFT_S=600

# ---- total wall clock, informational ----
# controlled SOFT + 2x notarize SOFT. Exceeding this is expected to be Apple
# most of the time; the per-phase rows say which.
BUILD_TOTAL_SOFT_S=1320
# HARD total = controlled HARD + both notarization HARDs (1500 + 2*600).
# 45 min. An over-an-hour build crosses this, and it is the only
# total-wall gate, because anything tighter is really a gate on Apple's queue.
BUILD_TOTAL_HARD_S=2700
